WEBVTT

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:07.904
Wherever a phone field shows a checked number, an icon shows the result.

00:00:07.904 --> 00:00:09.143
Open a contact:

00:00:09.143 --> 00:00:12.626
a green check means the service confirmed the number.

00:00:12.626 --> 00:00:15.400
Point at it to see the date of the check.

00:00:16.053 --> 00:00:17.922
A red icon means Invalid:

00:00:17.922 --> 00:00:20.756
the service says the number is not valid.

00:00:20.756 --> 00:00:24.193
Do not call it, and ask the customer for a new one.

00:00:24.682 --> 00:00:26.949
A warning sign means Failed:

00:00:26.949 --> 00:00:32.619
the check itself did not work, for example because the service was unavailable.

00:00:32.619 --> 00:00:38.622
The status is unknown, not invalid, and a failed check never marks a number invalid.

00:00:39.171 --> 00:00:42.899
A grey question mark means the number has not been checked yet.

00:00:42.899 --> 00:00:45.871
It is checked shortly after the contact is saved.

